1
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,120
Exactly.

2
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:37,280
We're in peacetime right now.

3
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,320
But war

4
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,240
won't wait for you to be ready.

5
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,240
Maybe tomorrow.

6
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,800
Maybe today.

7
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,240
Liang Hong,

8
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,400
you said I'm acting strange.

9
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,560
And I really am.

10
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,120
Because I don't know,

11
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,680
between these two,

12
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:57,480
how to find a balance.

13
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,760
Or this step...

14
00:01:59,040 --> 00:01:59,800
how big it needs to be

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,920
to be just right.

16
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:17,080
I share those same doubts you mentioned.

17
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,280
But no reform

18
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:29,040
is ever smooth sailing.

19
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,320
Because there's no experience to refer to,

20
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:33,240
we can only cross the river by feeling the stones.

21
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,000
Do you know why

22
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,640
I gave up the chance to go to Beijing

23
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:42,520
and stayed at the Wind Rider Battalion?

24
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,160
It's because I have confidence in you,

25
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,520
and in your Value Cube.

26
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:51,960
I want to witness the Value Cube's success.

27
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:55,720
The Guo Zijian I know

28
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,520
isn't someone who gets defeated easily.

29
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,120
Since we're going to be pioneers,

30
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,480
we have to bear pressure from all sides.

31
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,440
But I believe

32
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,880
everything will have a solution.

33
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,800
At the very least, I can promise

34
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,200
no matter what we face,

35
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,880
I will fight by your side.

36
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:29,560
Liang Hong,

37
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:31,880
I'm sorry.

38
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,120
It's just that

39
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,280
my heart feels heavy.

40
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:43,800
But I want to thank you.

41
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,000
You're right.

42
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,360
I can't let my emotions affect me.

43
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,360
Complaining

44
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,240
is the most useless thing to do.

45
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,920
Our Value Cube

46
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:57,720
will definitely start turning.

47
00:03:58,960 --> 00:03:59,920
No matter how hard it is,

48
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,440
we have to make it turn.

49
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:21,200
Chief.

50
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,320
Battalion Commander Guo,

51
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,480
We just arrived at the gate of the Wind Rider Battalion,

52
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,480
and you gave us a verbal storm.

53
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,040
I didn't expect that at all.

54
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:38,760
Reporter Luo,

55
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,440
I did say a lot of discouraging things,

56
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,560
but they truly are

57
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,200
my doubts as New-Type Battalion Commander.

58
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:48,760
I don't want to boast about

59
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,920
how advanced the Value Cube is.

60
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:52,200
I believe

61
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,920
time will prove everything.

62
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,680
But I hope even more

63
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,120
that you can take my questions today

64
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,360
back with you to think over,

65
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:00,560
and give me,

66
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,440
along with all the

67
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,360
troops of the Wind Rider Battalion,

68
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,080
an answer from a higher perspective.

69
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,160
Your request

70
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,560
is too demanding and difficult.

71
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,600
In the military field,

72
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,200
you're the chief expert reporter.

73
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:14,320
This won't stump you.

74
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:15,720
Unfortunately,

75
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,280
the Value Cube's security is too high.

76
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,000
The chief won't let me disclose anything,

77
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,640
and I don't dare to make things up.

78
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,120
However,

79
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,560
luckily I heard your true thoughts today.

80
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:26,960
I've gained quite a lot,

81
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,200
so I won't go back empty-handed.

82
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,160
Thank you for your understanding.

83
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,120
You shouldn't thank me.

84
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,360
You should thank your chief staff officer.

85
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:35,480
I believe

86
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,200
that with your hard work and cooperation,

87
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:38,720
we will surely witness

88
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,120
the impact of the Value Cube in action.

89
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,240
You flatter me.

90
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,400
Chief,

91
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,280
have Cmdr. Guo show me around Wind Rider.

92
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:48,440
We can chat some more.

93
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:49,400
What do you think?

94
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:50,600
I have no objections.

95
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:51,480
Inviting you here

96
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,960
means we have nothing to hide.

97
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:54,520
In that case, I think

98
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,200
we'd better not tag along,

99
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,560
in case our presence

100
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,760
makes Commander Guo hesitate to speak.

101
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:01,000
Chief,

102
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,440
please don't mock me.

103
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,920
I'll go back and write a self-criticism

104
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:06,120
regarding my recent ideological issues.

105
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,080
Write what?

106
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,880
A self-criticism.

107
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:10,680
I heard you.

108
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,040
Then I'll be waiting for it.

109
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,000
Yes, sir.

110
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,400
Not only will he write one,

111
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,480
I'll also write a self-criticism for you.

112
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,120
Now that the reporter is here,

113
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,760
you two are vying with each other.

114
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:23,360
Alright.

115
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,440
I'll be waiting for you both.

116
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,080
I've been in Wind Rider Battalion so long,

117
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,440
and it's only today

118
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,920
that I saw Commander Guo's true skills.

119
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,400
Our commander has always been skilled.

120
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:39,960
That's why I'm saying,

121
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:43,320
Commander Jiang and Chief Liu fall short.

122
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,200
This is also the reason

123
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,960
they could never handle Commander Guo.

124
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,400
Company Commander,

125
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,400
the more you talk, the less I understand.

126
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,040
What's there to not understand?

127
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,120
Think about it.

128
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,720
A reporter's interview.

129
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,800
Such an important promotional opportunity,

130
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,520
Deputy Liang chose Wind Rider Battalion.

131
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:05,960
The Hurricane Battalion was left out.

132
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:07,920
Why do you think that is?

133
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,240
Why?

134
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,960
Solid connections.

135
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,720
I think you're overthinking it.

136
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:19,120
You're just too simple-minded.

137
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,160
Battalion Commander Guo's move is called

138
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:22,880
victory by surprise.

139
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,040
Taking the unconventional path.

140
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,400
The moment the reporter arrived,

141
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:27,560
he and Officer Liang did a double act.

142
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:28,360
Wait.

143
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,840
They didn't put on a double act.

144
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,960
And they didn't intentionally draw

145
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:33,880
the reporter's attention.

146
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,160
Zhiqiang,

147
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,200
I know

148
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,400
you've always worked hard.

149
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,520
But if you can't be a little sharper,

150
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:48,200
you'll only be deputy company commander.

151
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,720
I don't think that far ahead.

152
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:52,280
Making it to company commander

153
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,640
would be a great honor for my family.

154
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,400
Your training plan for the next phase,

155
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:08,480
I've already reviewed it.

156
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:09,680
The pace is a bit slow.

157
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:10,720
Like a crawling turtle.

158
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,160
Chief, we want to be rabbits too,

159
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,120
running and jumping around.

160
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:14,600
But...

161
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:15,120
Alright.

162
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:16,840
Your thoughts...

163
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,400
you've made them very clear today.

164
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:21,280
Deputy Commander Suo is a bit strict.

165
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,320
But can you guarantee

166
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:24,800
that you have no problems yourselves?

167
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,600
Comrade Suo Jian'an is the representative

168
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,320
for your two battalions' off-base training.

169
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,000
He's under a tremendous amount of pressure.

170
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,000
Think about it.

171
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,120
Once your training exercises begin,

172
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,760
Every aspect, tangible or intangible,

173
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,360
it'll all be real combat scenarios.

174
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,720
A mistake in any link is no small matter.

175
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:42,760
Understood.

176
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,720
We did have some minor issues early on.

177
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,800
Minor issues?

178
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,440
I watched the footage.

179
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,280
Without the veteran commander behind you,

180
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,480
it would have been a major disaster.

181
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,680
The two company commanders also

182
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,080
adjusted their training plans accordingly.

183
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:57,960
The integration of equipment

184
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,800
requires a detailed plan.

185
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,640
The saying goes, bold but cautious.

186
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,440
This is the dialectic it speaks of.

187
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,760
Boldness stems from caution.

188
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:06,720
With caution,

189
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,520
you can grasp the full picture.

190
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:10,400
With this as a foundation,

191
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:11,440
no matter how bold you are,

192
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:12,640
it's never too much.

193
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:13,680
I understand.

194
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:15,120
Basically, we just can't be a hothead.

195
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:16,840
I think

196
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:19,320
nobody wants to admit they're a hothead.

197
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,680
Everyone feels they know what they're doing

198
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:23,160
and have figured everything out.

199
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:24,120
But,

200
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,760
when it comes to actual operation,

201
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,000
one problem pops up,

202
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,080
then another.

203
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:29,680
Brigade Commander,

204
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,040
are you talking about me?

205
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,800
Am I talking about you?

206
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:33,680
Think about it yourself.

207
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:35,760
Guo Zijian,

208
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,960
I handed nearly a thousand Wind Rider men

209
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,000
into your hands.

210
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,040
How you train them,

211
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,360
and to what extent,

212
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,280
to be honest,

213
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,840
I'm as unsure as you are.

214
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,560
I just want to tell you,

215
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,760
once the cube starts turning,

216
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,680
there's no giving up halfway.

217
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,600
The subjects you prepared,

218
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,400
those numbers, the equipment,

219
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:57,960
will all come alive.

220
00:09:58,920 --> 00:09:59,600
I hope

221
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,360
that within your Value Cube,

222
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:03,560
their full value can be realized.

223
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:06,200
Also,

224
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,560
I know

225
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:12,720
Wu Dongsheng has always been your hang-up.

226
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:16,760
Only you can untangle this hang-up.

227
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,000
What I want to tell you is,

228
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,240
all the troops of Wind Rider Battalion

229
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,080
are Wu Dongsheng.

230
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:26,080
They are all your irreplaceable comrades.

231
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,320
Safety issues on the training ground

232
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,120
have always been an iron chain

233
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:33,960
around the necks of frontline troops.

234
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:35,600
If anything goes wrong,

235
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,720
the ones held accountable

236
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,760
are never the ones who made the plans.

237
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,080
You are right, Chief.

238
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,840
There's a saying lately in the military.

239
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,200
"If an accident happens early in the year,

240
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:47,600
the whole year is wasted.

241
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,480
If it happens late, the year was wasted."

242
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:50,920
Even though everyone knows

243
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:54,280
that training safety and management safety

244
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:55,120
are two different things,

245
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,200
as soon as an accident happens,

246
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,040
these two things

247
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,400
become one and the same.

248
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,400
This iron chain

249
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,480
has brought many restrictions

250
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:06,040
to our combat-oriented training.

251
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:06,760
However,

252
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,360
we cannot let this chain make us

253
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,400
lower our standards.

254
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:11,960
Understood?

255
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:14,000
Recently, Military Commission leaders

256
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,560
regarding military training,

257
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,440
have significantly increased incentives.

258
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:21,600
This includes addressing this very issue.

259
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:22,960
That's great news!

260
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,960
Also, I must remind you,

261
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,080
when focusing on safety, some comrades

262
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:29,160
become overly cautious.

263
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,720
When policies change even slightly,

264
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,760
they immediately go complete hands-off.

265
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:35,960
Neither extreme will build good troops.

266
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,440
Scientific training

267
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,760
is a long road.

268
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,440
I also spoke with Deputy Commander Suo.

269
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:45,800
His management of you

270
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,000
will change in the future.

271
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:47,800
But you

272
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,680
must maintain enough respect for him.

273
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,360
You absolutely must not pay lip service.

274
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:51,880
Yes, sir.

275
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:52,200
Yes, sir.

276
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:53,560
Understood clearly.

277
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:54,600
Understood.

278
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,480
I also believe

279
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,400
you can definitely lead a unit

280
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,360
that can truly fight tough battles.

281
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,360
Rest assured, Chief.

282
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:03,960
I know what to do.

283
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:08,400
His words

284
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:10,320
were meant to cause trouble for you.

285
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,040
As for Guo Zijian,

286
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
if you say he's foolish,

287
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,680
he's smarter than anyone.

288
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:18,760
If you say he's smart,

289
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,440
sometimes he seems a bit foolish.

290
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,640
However,

291
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,360
no matter how you categorize him,

292
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,320
if you try to label him

293
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:31,720
as the type of

294
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,640
deeply scheming

295
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,400
and calculating person,

296
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:36,600
I disagree.

297
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,600
And I don't approve of you thinking so.

298
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,720
But the facts are right there.

299
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,200
Wasn't he doing this on purpose?

300
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,760
Enough, stop making wild guesses.

301
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,480
It's possible that this matter

302
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:48,920
is truly my responsibility.

303
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,120
I made a slight overcorrection.

304
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:52,480
Oh, come on.

305
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:54,960
You can't let him lead you astray.

306
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:56,920
There's no need to sign this.

307
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,280
Regarding the next phase of training,

308
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:00,680
Deputy Corps Commander Liang

309
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:01,960
once proposed

310
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:03,880
that the two battalions discuss it well,

311
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,240
and come up with an optimal plan.

312
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:07,000
Since the Chief has given instructions,

313
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:09,400
your department shouldn't interfere much.

314
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,000
All right then.

315
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,000
I'll be going now.

316
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:15,160
Okay.

317
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:19,120
Comrades,

318
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:21,040
for our next step,

319
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:24,600
on the coordinated use of all equipment,

320
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:27,280
firepower application for striking targets,

321
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,600
the optimal allocation of combat forces,

322
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:30,600
as well as

323
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:33,560
command coordination in combined ops,

324
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:35,440
we must prepare contingency plans early.

325
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:36,840
I know

326
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,840
for a formation with such high expertise,

327
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:43,040
headquarters used to provide the plans.

328
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,160
But this time,

329
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,720
our Wind Rider Battalion's training plan

330
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,280
is delegated by the army and brigade.

331
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,440
We have to come up with it ourselves.

332
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,560
So, what is our general approach?

333
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:52,760
Tell me your thoughts.

334
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:54,880
Battalion Commander,

335
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,000
we've been discussing the theory lately,

336
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:59,200
and in theory, these problems are solved.

337
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,360
Why our live-equipment training is poor,

338
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:02,120
I think,

339
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:03,320
is simply a lack of practice.

340
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,800
With such a large force and so much gear,

341
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,520
An engine's roar costs a fortune.

342
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:09,880
Besides,

343
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,640
using live ammo, aside from the cost,

344
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:13,040
definitely skyrockets the danger index.

345
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:14,760
So I was thinking,

346
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:16,640
before live-equipment joint training,

347
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,600
could we try simulation training first?

348
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:21,280
Simulation training?

349
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,880
Is that like playing a video game?

350
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:25,000
Right, it's roughly the same idea.

351
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:28,000
Our battalion could take all its gear,

352
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:29,280
and even the training grounds,

353
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:30,720
and fully digitize them for simulation.

354
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,040
For example,

355
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,160
the range of long-range rockets.

356
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,720
Depending on the different ammunition,

357
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,560
we can set it from 100 to 300 kilometers.

358
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,960
As long as the coordinates are set,

359
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,040
and a simulated projectile is fired,

360
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,360
the computer calculates the ammunition's

361
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,200
flight time,

362
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,280
trajectory,

363
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,120
impact area,

364
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,280
and its lethal effect.

365
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,320
Then, based on a specific algorithm,

366
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,240
the target area's

367
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,800
combat units and weapons equipment

368
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:50,840
would be eliminated from the battle.

369
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,200
This is no joke.

370
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:57,560
Data modeling alone is a massive task.

371
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:58,760
Actually,

372
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:00,240
currently on the market,

373
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:01,920
some large-scale real-time strategy games

374
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,120
have already partially fulfilled

375
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,280
the requirements for simulation training.

376
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,200
It's just that

377
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,320
their design is too entertainment-focused.

378
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:09,960
In reality,

379
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,120
our military's red-blue laser system,

380
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,280
as well as civilian

381
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,960
large shootout simulation facilities,

382
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:17,120
have initially achieved some functions.

383
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,960
I think if we integrate them all

384
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,320
and make improvements,

385
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,320
it is still achievable.

386
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,320
This...

387
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:36,640
won't work.

388
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:39,800
Deputy Brigade Commander,

389
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:42,440
before this plan was submitted to you,

390
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,400
it underwent multiple feasibility studies.

391
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,720
They all said it was feasible.

392
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:46,680
Let me tell you something.

393
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:48,440
In the military,

394
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:51,120
Secrecy is life.

395
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,920
Look at this project of yours.

396
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,240
It explicitly states

397
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:56,880
that all the parameters of our equipment

398
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,960
will be provided to civilian companies.

399
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,160
My goodness,

400
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,200
isn't this absurd?

401
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:04,840
These companies

402
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,720
are military-civilian integration units.

403
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:08,160
They are qualified for this.

404
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,520
The core data of the equipment...

405
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:11,160
We will definitely not give it to them.

406
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,320
You can't be careless, I'm telling you.

407
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:14,800
Espionage

408
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,000
is pervasive.

409
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,800
Leaks can happen anywhere.

410
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:20,920
Come here, look at this.

411
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:22,720
According to your requirements,

412
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,880
you'll have to install high-tech storage

413
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:26,640
and

414
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,120
analysis equipment in the future.

415
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:30,600
Then let me ask you,

416
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,080
in the future, wouldn't my

417
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,040
equipment performance,

418
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:34,920
my battalion and company tactics,

419
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,280
and my logistical capabilities

420
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,240
all be exposed to others?

421
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,920
Have you considered this issue?

422
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:42,280
We've drafted a non-disclosure agreement.

423
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,680
Once Value Cube research is successful,

424
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:47,200
the core database of the military version

425
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,480
will be operated solely by our unit.

426
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,680
Civilian entities will not be involved.

427
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:51,920
So this problem is

428
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,120
not difficult to solve.

429
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:56,440
Better safe than sorry.

430
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:57,520
In short,

431
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,640
I do not approve of this project.

432
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:00,800
The reason is very simple.

433
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,120
It's too far ahead of its time.

434
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,560
Like the old saying, it's too big a step.

435
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:06,880
Deputy Brigade Commander,

436
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,560
this kind of equipment

437
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,200
is just upgraded laser simulated combat.

438
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,480
The 404th Brigade's Blue Force detachment

439
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,040
has already started equipping it.

440
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:16,400
The 404th Brigade has it?

441
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,440
Good.

442
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,080
Here's an idea.

443
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:19,560
Go find Long Yuanshan.

444
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:21,520
Doesn't he think highly of you?

445
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,560
I'm leaving this to you.

446
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:24,480
You go to him,

447
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,560
and I'll pay the rental fee.

448
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,680
No, the situation is different.

449
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,560
This is best. Let's do it this way.

450
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:30,680
All right.

451
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:31,960
I have other matters to attend to.

452
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:35,640
Get the car ready,

453
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:42,480
I need to go out.

454
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:43,720
OK, OK, OK.

455
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:44,440
Yes, sir.

456
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,000
Hello, Battalion Commander Guo.

457
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,000
How did your talk with Deputy Suo go?

458
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,120
No matter what I say,

459
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,200
Deputy Commander Suo has one response.

460
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,040
Take too big a step, and you'll stumble.

461
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,480
How are we supposed to innovate like this?

462
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:19,160
Actually,

463
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,960
there's a process to everything.

464
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:23,920
As long as there is a process,

465
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:27,280
there will be room for us to maneuver.

466
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:29,000
Personally, I think

467
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:30,400
our technical R&D

468
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,440
must still be pushed forward.

469
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:33,560
If anything goes wrong,

470
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,040
I'll take responsibility.

471
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,160
The most crucial thing is

472
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:40,120
that the results of our R&D

473
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,680
must be ahead of the curve.

474
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,560
If Deputy Cmdr. Suo is our Gatekeeper,

475
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,560
he'll open the door for us when it's time.

476
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:47,680
Because this is a win-win situation.

477
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:49,840
Besides, what he repeatedly emphasized is

478
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:51,720
not to take too big a step.

479
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:54,720
He didn't say we can't move forward.

480
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:56,680
We can submit for approval first.

481
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:57,720
I'll write the report.

482
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,360
Exactly.

483
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,560
If not a dead end, we can make it work.

484
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,000
If the report gets approved,

485
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,560
we'll need to finalize a partner company.

486
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,080
I suggest contacting Military Dream Group.

487
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:11,240
With their qualifications and strength,

488
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,480
they are the most suitable choice.

489
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:15,080
But from approval to payment,

490
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:16,280
the process will take a long time.

491
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,200
With our tight schedule,

492
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,040
without an advance payment,

493
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:20,320
there's no way to start R&D.

494
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,400
What should we do about this?

495
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:33,160
I'll handle it.

496
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:39,000
My brother is offering us pie in the sky.

497
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,880
He didn't mention a word about the budget.

498
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,320
He won't even pay the project's advance.

499
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,320
Right.

500
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,120
Military Dream has always been

501
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,760
an enterprise with dreams and passion.

502
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:51,480
But we can't just dream and not charge.

503
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:54,240
Don't you know your brother by now?

504
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:55,840
That silly boy...

505
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,800
He just doesn't understand some procedures.

506
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,320
You should remind him.

507
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,000
He tricked you.

508
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:03,640
He understands better than anyone.

509
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:06,160
He hasn't even returned my last favor.

510
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:07,360
This time,

511
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:10,000
he wants to get something for nothing.

512
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,120
How is that possible?

513
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:16,280
Wind Rider Battalion is a new force.

514
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,160
Besides, the defense budget isn't lacking.

515
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,840
Why would they hold back his funds?

516
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:24,080
If it weren't for these reasons,

517
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:25,640
I would've stopped talking to them.

518
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,680
But as for this plan,

519
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:30,280
I don't see any sincerity to cooperate.

520
00:20:31,760 --> 00:20:33,320
Dad, I have an idea.

521
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,080
Tell me.

522
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,760
Let's leave them hanging for a while.

523
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:40,160
We'll start the project when there's money.

524
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,120
Whenever they have money,

525
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,080
we'll start it.

526
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:44,200
What kind of idea is that?

527
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,560
Aren't you just keeping them in suspense?

528
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,440
Then you tell me what to do.

529
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,480
I think your brother might be in trouble.

530
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:54,600
How about this?

531
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:59,000
Our group will advance the money first.

532
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:00,800
The responsibility

533
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:03,400
will fall directly on me.

534
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:06,280
I knew this would be the outcome.

535
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:08,200
Well, we can't let your brother struggle.

536
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:09,800
Fine.

537
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,640
You've given the order, so I'll get to work.

538
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:16,040
But if this project loses money...

539
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:18,760
Over all these years,

540
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:21,240
it won't be the first time I lost money.

541
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,800
We are a defense contractor now.

542
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,960
As long as the army can win battles,

543
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:27,840
for us common folks,

544
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,720
there's only one outcome.

545
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:31,040
What outcome?

546
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:32,160
A guaranteed win.

547
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:36,280
Bro.

548
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:37,840
For this matter,

549
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:39,840
Dad is covering for you.

550
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:42,080
If we develop it

551
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:42,960
according to your needs,

552
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,720
you need to send staff

553
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,680
over to coordinate

554
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,760
and participate in R&D.

555
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:48,080
How's that?

556
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:52,760
No problem.

557
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:53,600
Bro,

558
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:56,320
you're leeching off us for the state.

559
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:57,560
This is the last time.

560
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,080
If this continues, we'll go bankrupt.

561
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:02,080
Are you fine with letting me live on air?

562
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,480
If we really go bankrupt,

563
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,080
it's fine.

564
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,680
I'll support you from now on.

565
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:08,080
Even if I'm willing,

566
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:10,200
my future sister-in-law might not be.

567
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:11,880
Alright, stop joking around.

568
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:12,680
I'm hanging up.

569
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:16,080
Wu Dongsheng.

570
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:19,240
I drove, so let me take you back.

571
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:20,120
Thanks,

572
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:21,560
but no need.

573
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:31,160
How did it go?

574
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:32,560
How was the talk?

575
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:33,600
It's settled.

576
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:35,560
But,

577
00:22:35,920 --> 00:22:37,560
Officer Liang needs to make a sacrifice.

578
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,400
What sacrifice?

579
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:40,960
Sacrificing a month's leave

580
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:42,600
to join the R&D at Military Dream.

581
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,520
That's no sacrifice at all.

582
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:45,720
No problem.

583
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:13,000
This detail right here

584
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:14,320
still needs some improvement.

585
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,200
Wu Dongsheng.

586
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:18,040
Staff Officer Liang.

587
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:20,640
I'll leave you to it.

588
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:22,600
You...

589
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,840
Looks like you're doing well now.

590
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,080
I'm doing great.

591
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,880
You work here?

592
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:40,800
Yeah.

593
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:42,320
Before,

594
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:44,320
Military Dream Group reached out to me.

595
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,400
I always found it pretty strange

596
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:48,520
until you showed up today.

597
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,160
Now it makes sense.

598
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,160
Battalion Commander Guo...

599
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:54,600
Anyway,

600
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:56,720
I appreciate his kindness.

601
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:59,160
With a good battalion commander like him,

602
00:24:00,160 --> 00:24:01,400
I'm really quite lucky.

603
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:03,200
It's not just you.

604
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:05,440
We're all lucky to have him as commander.

605
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:27,800
I've been gone for just over a month,

606
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,160
but the mountains have changed so much.

607
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:30,160
The flowers have already bloomed.

608
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:31,000
Yeah.

609
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:33,160
Everyone is really looking forward

610
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:35,080
to your simulation system going online.

611
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:38,800
Actually, I've always had a question.

612
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,160
What question?

613
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,680
How did you convince Military Dream Group

614
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:43,520
when we haven't paid

615
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:44,920
a single cent,

616
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:46,360
to still take the lead and help us?

617
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:47,560
Also,

618
00:24:49,760 --> 00:24:50,560
Wu Dongsheng.

619
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,280
You met Wu Dongsheng?

620
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:56,920
He told me to say thank you to you.

621
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,400
I still couldn't keep it from him, huh.

622
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,040
Did you meet Chen Hanxiao?

623
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:06,440
I did.

624
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,320
The chairman of Military Dream Group.

625
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:11,480
All this is because of his support.

626
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:13,120
He's a veteran who participated

627
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:15,440
in the border conflicts back in the day.

628
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:17,720
He's also devoted to our national defense,

629
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:19,240
a true hardcore fan.

630
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:24,320
So it's really because of him?

631
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:25,360
Not because of Chen Xiaoshan?

632
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:27,200
Chen Xiaoshan?

633
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:28,320
What?

634
00:25:28,840 --> 00:25:30,640
Did she take all the credit for herself?

635
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:32,160
Don't listen to her brag.

636
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:33,600
She's just an errand runner.

637
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:34,920
Battalion Commander Guo.

638
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:36,760
That's not a very objective assessment.

639
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,800
If it weren't for her recently,

640
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:40,520
we wouldn't have progressed so smoothly.

641
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:42,920
You guys are practically family now.

642
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:45,640
In another week,

643
00:25:45,760 --> 00:25:47,040
Ms. Chen will bring a few

644
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:48,400
technicians from her production unit

645
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,280
to install the first batch of samples.

646
00:25:50,600 --> 00:25:51,480
If the technical testing

647
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:52,800
and data collection are successful,

648
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,600
it can soon be deployed for the battalion.

649
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,960
That's great news.

650
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:00,240
Thanks for your hard work, Officer Liang.

651
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:01,280
Don't mention it.

652
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:07,200
Look.

653
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:09,080
There's also a large platform here.

654
00:26:11,080 --> 00:26:11,760
The soldiers

655
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:14,240
often come here to enjoy the scenery.

656
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:16,320
At night, you can even see the stars.

657
00:26:17,360 --> 00:26:18,400
The air is really nice here.

658
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:18,880
Isn't it?

659
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:22,080
This Guo Zijian.

660
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:23,760
Doesn't he know I have a delivery today?

661
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:25,400
I told him before.

662
00:26:25,840 --> 00:26:26,920
Look what time it is!

663
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:28,360
Does he have any concept of time?

664
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:31,040
Cmdr. Guo is usually training right now.

665
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:32,200
It's his daily routine.

666
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:33,640
But he should be wrapping up soon.

667
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:36,720
So I came at a bad time, then?

668
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:37,960
Squad Leader Hong!

669
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:38,400
Here!

670
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:39,640
Go find Battalion Commander Guo.

671
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:40,880
If he's done with his training,

672
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:41,760
tell him to get here as soon as possible.

673
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:42,760
Don't keep Ms. Chen waiting too long.

674
00:26:42,760 --> 00:26:43,040
Yes, sir.

675
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:53,200
Staff Officer Liang.

676
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,440
Do you ever feel like

677
00:26:55,640 --> 00:26:57,800
Commander Guo is hard to get along with?

678
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:01,480
Why do you ask?

679
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:05,040
He became a commander at such a young age.

680
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,560
Of Wind Rider Battalion, watched by all.

681
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:10,280
Military media praised him highly recently.

682
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:11,560
Anyone would get cocky.

683
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:12,520
He wouldn't.

684
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:14,680
Commander Guo wouldn't let things like this

685
00:27:14,680 --> 00:27:15,440
make him arrogant.

686
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,160
You really defend him.

687
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,760
I'm just telling the truth.

688
00:27:21,360 --> 00:27:23,000
Don't be nervous. I didn't mean anything.

689
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:27,520
Staff Officer Liang,

690
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:29,640
how long have you been in the army?

691
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:30,920
Twelve years.

692
00:27:31,120 --> 00:27:31,960
You're a veteran.

693
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:33,720
I couldn't tell.

694
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:36,080
Maybe it's because

695
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:37,840
I haven't been out of school for long.

696
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:39,520
I've been at the academy all this time.

697
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,880
You must have a lot of guys chasing you.

698
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:48,040
No guys are chasing me.

699
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:49,240
Impossible.

700
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:51,920
You're so pretty and educated.

701
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:53,720
There must be a lot of guys

702
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:54,800
going out of their way to approach you.

703
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:56,840
Approach me?

704
00:27:57,040 --> 00:27:58,000
That definitely happens.

705
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,920
When I was at the academy,

706
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:02,240
a lot of classmates would come to me

707
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:04,080
to do scientific research together.

708
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:05,280
And when I came to the unit,

709
00:28:05,280 --> 00:28:06,800
I also trained with the soldiers.

710
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:10,480
But none of that counts as chasing, right?

711
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:15,280
Commander Guo has a bumpy love life.

712
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:16,600
What did you say?

713
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:19,360
I said Battalion Commander Guo's reform

714
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,080
faces a bumpy road ahead.

715
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:23,480
He even told you about this?

716
00:28:23,480 --> 00:28:24,720
Of course.

717
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:26,800
If he didn't use this sympathy ploy,

718
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:27,960
would my dad let him buy on credit?

719
00:28:28,760 --> 00:28:30,200
Seems you've known each other a long time.

720
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:32,520
We've known each other since birth.

721
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:33,880
Chen Xiaoshan.

722
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,560
Gossiping about me again?

723
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:39,040
I wouldn't dare say anything about you.

724
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,160
I'm your creditor,

725
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:41,920
yet you left me hanging here so long, huh?

726
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:44,080
Have you no self-awareness as a debtor?

727
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:47,360
You're our Unofficial Logistics Captain now.

728
00:28:47,360 --> 00:28:48,680
How could I dare neglect you?

729
00:28:49,080 --> 00:28:50,040
I just finished training.

730
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:51,200
Good to know.

731
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:52,520
Let me report to you.

732
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:54,120
The trial products have arrived.

733
00:28:54,800 --> 00:28:55,560
I saw them.

734
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:56,680
Highly efficient.

735
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:57,600
Worthy of praise.

736
00:28:58,760 --> 00:28:59,800
To be honest,

737
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:01,760
the technical content of this isn't high.

738
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:04,560
It's mostly a few tech vendors borrowing from

739
00:29:04,560 --> 00:29:06,560
the core of military games on the market

740
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:08,080
and industry technological achievements.

741
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:09,480
They also referenced

742
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:12,240
the existing combat systems in your unit.

743
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:14,800
In short, everyone has their specialty.

744
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:16,160
But for

745
00:29:16,160 --> 00:29:18,400
a computer expert like Officer Liang,

746
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:19,120
it won't be hard to pick up.

747
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,120
Ms. Chen, you're being too modest.

748
00:29:22,320 --> 00:29:24,600
Actually, researchers at Military Dream

749
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,600
made many improvements to our project.

750
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:28,240
This also includes

751
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:30,240
much of their independent IP.

752
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:33,000
Anyway, I got the job done for you.

753
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:34,720
How are you going to thank me?

754
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,120
The scenery here is nice, isn't it?

755
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:40,160
Once our

756
00:29:40,160 --> 00:29:42,120
equipment installation report is approved,

757
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:43,400
I'll take you mountain climbing.

758
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:44,560
It's a deal.

759
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:45,640
Staff Officer Liang, join us.

760
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:46,680
Staff Officer Liang will be my witness.

761
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:47,800
I won't join you,

762
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:48,800
but I can be your witness.

763
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:49,960
Commander.

764
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:51,160
Do you want to say it again?

765
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:52,280
Let me grab my phone to record it.

766
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:54,440
You must be tired.

767
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:55,800
Let me take you to the tent to rest.

768
00:29:55,800 --> 00:29:56,160
Let's go.

769
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,080
What are you doing?

770
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:33,080
Sneaking around like a thief.

771
00:30:34,120 --> 00:30:34,880
Watch your mouth.

772
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:37,760
Keep your hands off.

773
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:41,120
I'm just checking if it's locked tight.

774
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:45,480
I need to discuss something with you.

775
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:46,440
Go ahead.

776
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:53,640
Let me use it too.

777
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:55,960
Share the wealth, right?

778
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:58,360
Sure.

779
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:00,040
But I have a condition.

780
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:01,360
Go ahead.

781
00:31:02,520 --> 00:31:03,440
You come with me

782
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:05,480
to report to Deputy Commander Suo.

783
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:06,720
That's impossible.

784
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,720
Impossible?

785
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:09,160
What are you trying to do?

786
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:10,480
Want to use me as your pawn again, right?

787
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:12,200
Didn't I get yelled at enough last time?

788
00:31:13,040 --> 00:31:13,720
Let me tell you, this time,

789
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:15,400
go apply for it yourself.

790
00:31:16,120 --> 00:31:16,920
Once it's approved,

791
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,120
I'll just tag along

792
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:23,560
and reap the benefits.

793
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:25,880
How can you be so shameless?

794
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:27,040
If I weren't shameless,

795
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:29,200
how could I deal with you, Guo Zijian?

796
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:30,320
Am I right?

797
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:33,120
Good luck.

798
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:35,480
I'm rooting for you.

799
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:36,400
Scram.

800
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:46,840
No.

801
00:31:47,360 --> 00:31:48,720
Before the official documents are issued,

802
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:49,640
absolutely not.

803
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:51,000
Deputy Commander,

804
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:53,720
since the equipment is already made,

805
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:55,560
can't we at least test it?

806
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:58,400
Approving R&D doesn't mean approving tests.

807
00:31:58,440 --> 00:31:59,200
Let me tell you,

808
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,680
whenever you do anything,

809
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:02,960
you must follow proper procedures.

810
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:04,280
You can't rush things.

811
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:05,920
We just want to test it.

812
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:07,320
If it works, we use it.

813
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,000
If it doesn't, we drop it.

814
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:10,720
It's absolutely not allowed.

815
00:32:11,520 --> 00:32:12,080
Deputy Commander,

816
00:32:12,080 --> 00:32:12,960
here's the situation.

817
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:14,480
Recently,

818
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:17,400
Liang Hong discussed it with experts

819
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:19,240
and completed the top-level design.

820
00:32:19,880 --> 00:32:21,520
This equipment is all external.

821
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:22,480
To our equipment,

822
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:24,520
it won't cause any physical damage.

823
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:26,120
Listen to me, Guo Zijian,

824
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:29,480
is it because a few reporters

825
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:30,800
publicized you recently

826
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:33,240
that you've lost your bearings now?

827
00:32:34,080 --> 00:32:35,800
You don't know your place anymore, do you?

828
00:32:36,120 --> 00:32:37,200
Good heavens.

829
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:38,560
You think you're so capable now.

830
00:32:38,720 --> 00:32:40,120
You're even modifying equipment.

831
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:41,120
Don't get cocky.

832
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:42,840
Dare touch one piece of my equipment,

833
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:44,160
I won't let you off the hook.

834
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:46,080
Deputy Commander,

835
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:48,520
when did I ever get cocky?

836
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:50,000
The Military Dream Group

837
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:51,520
funded the initial design

838
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:52,960
without asking the military for a cent.

839
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:54,960
They contacted the manufacturers

840
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,000
and design units on their own.

841
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:57,600
Their executives are here today.

842
00:32:58,120 --> 00:32:59,360
Why don't you have a private chat with her?

843
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:01,600
Just treat it as learning about the gear.

844
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:02,760
Why would I see her?

845
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:04,800
What do I need to see them for?

846
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:06,320
Let me tell you,

847
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:07,800
this batch of equipment

848
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:09,320
not only cannot be installed,

849
00:33:09,560 --> 00:33:11,360
but must be sealed immediately.

850
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:12,840
Sealed?

851
00:33:13,440 --> 00:33:14,960
But those are their products.

852
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:16,440
Are you stupid or something?

853
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:20,160
Didn't Liang Hong study with them a month?

854
00:33:20,640 --> 00:33:21,480
Does this equipment

855
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:23,080
contain our information?

856
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:25,240
Or the parameters of our equipment?

857
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,360
That's hard to say.

858
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:28,280
Don't worry. Liang Hong didn't leak

859
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:29,840
our information and parameters.

860
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:32,240
Excuse me, Commander.

861
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:34,400
